From: Surface Pro 11 Fedora build
Subject: [PATCH] stub: start the kernel without LoadImage() and read the initramfs from the ESP

Two changes for the Surface Pro 11 (firmware of 2026, shim 16.1), where an image started with Secure Boot on
must not go through shim's LoadImage(): shim verifies the image and then does not return.

linux.c: the stub copies the kernel's sections itself and jumps to it, also with Secure Boot on and shim's
loader present. The kernel is part of the stub's own image, which shim has verified as a whole when the boot
loader started it. sp11_stub=shim-loader on the command line restores the unpatched path, for a test of a
later shim.

stub.c: GRUB's chainloader passes no initrd, and the kernel's own reading of initrd= files does not work with
this firmware. With sp11_initrd=<path> on the command line the stub reads that file from the volume the image
was started from, in the chunks chunked_read() uses for firmware that cannot read a large file in one call,
and hands it over in the place of an initrd of the boot loader. Without the file the kernel is not started.

sp11_stub=debug raises the log level: the stub then reports each of these steps and pauses before the kernel.

Applies to systemd 262.1 (src/boot). LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the files it changes.
